  "answer": "John Clayton and Arthur Cecil were the joint managers of the Court Theatre, where 'Dandy Dick' was produced. They commissioned the play from Arthur W. Pinero, and Clayton was involved in its development, including hearing Pinero read the first two acts and encouraging the new idea. Clayton also acted in the play as the Dean, and Cecil acted as Blore. The production was part of their management, and Clayton later transferred the play to Toole's Theatre and toured with it until his death.",
